<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Thebes</h1><p class="st-meta">900 BCE – 146 BCE (approx.) · capital Thebes</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Leading city of Boeotia whose generals Epaminondas and Pelopidas broke Spartan power at Leuctra in 371 BCE and briefly made Thebes the first power of Greece.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Thebes grew from the Mycenaean palace town on the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mycenaean-kingdom-of-thebes">Kadmeia</a>, surviving the collapse c. 1200 BCE. In the Archaic period it became the chief city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boeotia">Boeotia</a> and, from the late 6th century BCE, the head of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/boeotian-league">Boeotian League</a>, competing with Orchomenus and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/plataea">Plataea</a> for leadership.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thebes-greece">Thebes</a> was ruled mostly by landowning oligarchies. It sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> in 480 BCE and was punished after <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/plataea">Plataea</a>, then backed <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sparta">Sparta</a> in the Peloponnesian War. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a> seized the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mycenaean-kingdom-of-thebes">Kadmeia</a> in 382 BCE, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pelopidas">Pelopidas</a> liberated it in 379 BCE. With the Sacred Band and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epaminondas">Epaminondas's</a> deep <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phalanx">phalanx</a>, Thebes won at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-leuctra">Leuctra</a>, freed <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/messene">Messenia</a> and founded <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/megalopolis">Megalopolis</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epaminondas">Epaminondas</a> died at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mantinea">Mantinea</a> in 362 BCE, Theban power faded. Defeated with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/athens">Athens</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-chaeronea-338-bce">Chaeronea</a> in 338 BCE, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thebes-greece">Thebes</a> revolted and was razed by Alexander in 335 BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cassander">Cassander</a> rebuilt it in 316 BCE, and it passed under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 146 BCE.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/thebes.jpg" alt="Thebes" width="320" height="240"><figcaption>Image: Chabe01 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vue_Nord_Ville_-_Th%C3%A8bes_(GR03)_-_2022-03-21_-_3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>900 BCE – 146 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century-bce">10th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Thebes</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Pelopidas, Epaminondas</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Greek religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Boeotian Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Thebai, Classical Thebes</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-523&amp;focus=thebes" aria-label="Thebes on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5260 801 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Thebes lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5580 1057L5569 1054M5580 1057L5548 987M5580 1057L5304 942M5580 1057L5571 1052M5580 1057L5553 1087"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5569 1054h0M5548 987h0M5304 942h0M5571 1052h0M5553 1087h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5580 1057h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5580 1057h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=-523&amp;focus=thebes">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

